    {
      "to": "Amara Okafor <amara@finchdata.co>",
      "subject": "Re: jac-cloud on Kubernetes?",
      "message": "Hi Amara,\n\nThanks for reaching out \u2014 happy to help as you evaluate jac-cloud for Q4.\n\n1. EKS / self-managed Kubernetes: Yes, jac-cloud can be deployed on your own Kubernetes cluster, including AWS EKS. We provide Helm charts and container images that you can install into an existing cluster, so you retain control over your infrastructure and networking. If it would help, I can share our deployment guide and sample values.yaml for EKS-specific considerations (IAM roles for service accounts, ALB ingress, etc.).\n\n2. Walker horizontal scaling: jac-cloud does not currently auto-scale walker replicas out of the box. Replica management is left to you via standard Kubernetes primitives \u2014 typically a Deployment with an HPA based on CPU/custom metrics. We can walk you through recommended scaling configurations and any walker-specific considerations for your workload.\n\nIf it's useful, I'd be happy to set up a short technical call with our platform team to go deeper on both points and your specific Q4 requirements.\n\nBest,\nJason\nJaseci Team"
    },
